From 0baefaf88dcb4b8c69b61312c5411a474f89671c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix <52862870+devilAPI@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:35:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 27/28] media: i2c: add Samsung S5K2T8 image sensor driver

V4L2 driver for the Samsung S5K2T8 20 MP raw sensor, the rear camera
of the ZTE Axon 7. Four MIPI CSI-2 lanes, 24 MHz MCLK, SGRBG10.

Register sequences come from the sensor library of the phone's stock
camera stack: four init blocks (with their 1/1/15 ms delays) and three
of its modes: 5952x3348 at 30 fps (834 MHz link), 2976x1674 binned at
30 fps (300 MHz) and 1920x1080 at 60 fps (498 MHz). Exposure, analogue
gain (0x20 = 1x, up to 16x), vblank, flips and test patterns are
exposed as controls. Chip id register 0x0000 reads 0x2148.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FVN6i64chehV1XxwjxyaGp
